WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.320
- [Narrator] This is a
giant praying mantis.

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:06.350
It's located here, in Las Vegas, Nevada.

00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:07.806
But it's not located on the strip,

00:00:07.806 --> 00:00:11.090
the place that most people
think of when they think Vegas.

00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:13.325
Today, we're venturing off the beaten path

00:00:13.325 --> 00:00:15.230
with the help of three people.

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:16.063
- Hi.

00:00:16.063 --> 00:00:16.896
- Hi.

00:00:16.896 --> 00:00:17.755
- Hi.
- [Narrator] To three places

00:00:17.755 --> 00:00:21.453
that are single-handedly
keeping Vegas weird.

00:00:28.476 --> 00:00:30.250
This is Tim Arnold.

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:31.806
He's the director of stuff and things

00:00:31.806 --> 00:00:34.579
at the Pinball Hall of Fame in Las Vegas.

00:00:34.579 --> 00:00:37.533
- Pinball Hall of Fame is
an old auto parts store

00:00:37.533 --> 00:00:40.532
with a bunch of pinball machines
we dug out of dumpsters.

00:00:40.532 --> 00:00:43.322
No, no, no, it's a marvelous museum

00:00:43.322 --> 00:00:45.287
full of antique treasures that have been

00:00:45.287 --> 00:00:47.556
lovingly restored to
their original condition

00:00:47.556 --> 00:00:51.403
that we actually let the
public come in and play.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:57.700
We have games from the '30s
on up to today's modern games.

00:00:57.763 --> 00:01:00.490
I've seen people walking down an aisle

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:02.840
full of pinball machines
and they'll stop dead.

00:01:04.287 --> 00:01:06.920
The first time I kissed a girl was,

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:11.543
I was playing that game, and I
can't believe it's here again!

00:01:15.807 --> 00:01:18.725
This is not something
that can be digitized

00:01:18.725 --> 00:01:21.593
and sent down the pipes on the internet.

00:01:24.113 --> 00:01:26.907
This is something that only
exists in the real world

00:01:26.907 --> 00:01:29.791
and the only place to play it is here.

00:01:29.791 --> 00:01:31.740
- [Narrator] Okay, Tim, we're sold.

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:33.350
Who's got change for a dollar?

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:34.544
- My name's Kristine Reynolds.

00:01:34.544 --> 00:01:35.723
- [Narrator] She's the general manager

00:01:35.723 --> 00:01:37.650
at Downtown Container Park.

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:40.740
- Which is completely made
of shipping containers!

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:42.903
We wanted to re-use materials instead

00:01:42.903 --> 00:01:44.886
of just building from scratch.

00:01:44.886 --> 00:01:47.069
Container Park prides
itself on helping out

00:01:47.069 --> 00:01:48.997
Mom and Pop-type of brands.

00:01:48.997 --> 00:01:51.800
- [Narrator] Their unusual
shops, like Kappa Toys,

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:53.893
which specializes in throwback toys.

00:01:53.893 --> 00:01:56.980
And there's exceptional
grub to be had, too.

00:01:56.980 --> 00:01:59.760
And let's not forget about the mantis.

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:02.380
And this guy, who makes her move.

00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:04.227
Our last stop in downtown Las Vegas

00:02:04.227 --> 00:02:07.597
is a totally novel, literary adventure.

00:02:07.597 --> 00:02:09.120
- I am Drew Cohen.

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:11.640
My husband and I own The
Writer's Block together,

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:14.400
so you could say we're a
Pop and Pop establishment.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.535
We have a lot of kooky installations

00:02:16.535 --> 00:02:18.283
and objects in the store.

00:02:18.283 --> 00:02:21.600
We have an antique letter press from 1890.

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:24.711
We have a machine called
Bearsho who will produce

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:27.790
a haiku on demand for 25 cents.

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:30.504
We have a mailbox that
belongs to the king pigeon,

00:02:30.504 --> 00:02:32.915
and you can leave a
question in an envelope

00:02:32.915 --> 00:02:35.292
and return in one week for your answer.

00:02:35.292 --> 00:02:36.744
- [Narrator] And it all goes to support

00:02:36.744 --> 00:02:39.984
free writing classes for local students.

00:02:39.984 --> 00:02:41.277
So there you have it.

00:02:41.277 --> 00:02:43.066
Three delightfully strange places

00:02:43.066 --> 00:02:47.079
you can only find off
the beaten path in Vegas.

00:02:47.079 --> 00:02:49.340
- This city is a very eccentric one.

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:52.381
You can encounter a lot of really
wacko and awesome businesses

00:02:52.381 --> 00:02:55.001
if you are willing to
venture out a little bit.

00:02:55.001 --> 00:02:58.030
- [Kristine] If you want to
do shopping, there's shopping.

00:02:58.030 --> 00:02:59.730
The night life here is amazing.

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:04.349
- It really is something you
can't see in your hometown,

00:03:04.349 --> 00:03:07.590
and that's the definition
of why you come to Vegas.

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:10.721
It has dancing fountains
and pinball museums

00:03:10.721 --> 00:03:13.426
and all sorts of goofy stuff.

00:03:13.426 --> 00:03:15.800
- [Narrator] So next time you're in Vegas,

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:17.283
try straying from the strip.

